libspectrum 1.7.0
=================

libspectrum is a library which is designed to make the input and
output of ZX Spectrum emulator files slightly easier than it would be
otherwise. It should hopefully compile and run on Unix-based systems,
Win32 and Mac OS X.

Currently supported are:

* Snapshots: .z80, .szx, .sna (all read/write), .zxs, .sp., .snp and
  +D snapshots (read only).
* Tape images: .tzx, .tap, .spc, .sta, .ltp and .pzx (read/write); CSW v1/v2
  (read) and v2 (write); Warajevo .tap and Z80Em (read only).
  PZX writing supports native blocks and ROM/turbo/pure-data conversion;
  unsupported blocks are rejected (see doc/libspectrum.txt).
* Input recordings: .rzx (read/write).
* Disk images: .dsk (both plain and extended), .d40, .d80, .fdi, .img,
  .mgt, .opd, .sad, .scl, .td0, .trd and .udi (identification only).
* Timex cartridges: .dck (read only).
* IDE hard disk images: .hdf (read/write).
* Microdrive cartridge images: .mdr (read/write).

libspectrum is built with CMake (3.x is not enough: 4.2 or newer is
required) and needs Python 3 and a C23 compiler. On Unix and Mac OS X,
compiling libspectrum should just be as easy as

$ cmake -S . -B build
$ cmake --build build

and then `cmake --install build' should install it in `/usr/local'
ready for use on your system. If you want to install it somewhere other
than `/usr/local', give the `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=DIR' option to
`cmake' to install it under `DIR'. Once installed, some work may still
be necessary to ensure that the runtime linker can find libspectrum.
For example, on some Linux systems you may need to run `ldconfig' as
root after installing (for example `sudo ldconfig') before newly
installed libraries in `/usr/local/lib' are found.

Useful options (all given as -DNAME=VALUE):

  ZLIB_SUPPORT, BZIP2_SUPPORT   use zlib / bzip2 (default ON; fetched and
                                built if not found on the system)
  LIBGCRYPT_SUPPORT             RZX signing support via libgcrypt (ON)
  WAV_SUPPORT                   WAV support via libaudiofile or the native
                                macOS frameworks (ON)
  USE_FAKE_GLIB                 use the bundled GLib replacement instead
                                of GLib (default ON on Windows)
  BUILD_SHARED_LIBS             build a shared library (ON)
  LIBSPECTRUM_BUILD_TESTS       build the test suite; run it with `ctest'
                                from the build directory (OFF)

For details on the functions available, see `doc/libspectrum.txt'.
Maintainer release notes are in `doc/releasing.md'.

libspectrum is made available under the GNU General Public License,
which means that it is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,
but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
